rySubjects":["Science","Biography"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"The book primarily explores themes within medicine and public health through the lens of gene therapy while also capturing scientific advancements and the personal narrative of the Heywood brothers.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"c23f7593e079db1abf208a434c9f68c0f9139a9af2d0ff92c0e7d21273639667","summary":"From Jonathan Weiner, Pulitzer Prize-winning author of The Beak of the Finch, comes His Brother's Keeper -- the story of a young entrepreneur who gambles on the risky science of gene therapy to try to save his brother's life.Stephen Heywood was twenty-nine years old when he learned that he was dying of ALS -- Lou Gehrig's disease. Almost overnight his older brother, Jamie, turned himself into a genetic engineer in a quixotic race to cure the incurable. His Brother's Keeper is a powerful account of their story, as they travel together to the edge of medicine.The book brings home for all of us the hopes and fears of the new biology. In this dramatic and suspenseful narrative, Jonathan Weiner gives us a remarkable portrait of science and medicine today. We learn about gene therapy, stem cells, brain vaccines, and other novel treatments for such nerve-death diseases as ALS, Alzheimer's, and Parkinson's -- diseases that afflict millions, and touch the lives of many more.It turns out that the author has a personal stake in the story as well. When he met the Heywood brothers, his own mother was dying of a rare nerve-death disease. The Heywoods' gene therapist offered to try to save her, too.\"The Heywoods' story taught me many things about the nature of healing in the new millennium,\" Weiner writes.","publicationYear":2004,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Science","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Nonfiction","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Patients","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Brothers","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Family relationships","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biotechnology","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Genetic engineering","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Nature, effect of human beings on","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Habitat (ecology)","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Family Relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Genetic Therapy","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-his-brother-s-keeper-a-story-from-the-edge-of-medicine-jonathan-weiner"}],"displaySummary":"From Jonathan Weiner, Pulitzer Prize-winning author of The Beak of the Finch, comes His Brother's Keeper -- the story of a young entrepreneur who gambles on the risky science of gene therapy to try to save his brother's life.Stephen Heywood was twenty-nine years old when he learned that he was dying of ALS -- Lou Gehrig's disease. Almost overnight his older brother, Jamie, turned himself into a genetic engineer in a quixotic race to cure the incurable. His Brother's Keeper is a powerful account of their story, as they travel together to the edge of medicine.The book brings home for all of us the hopes and fears of the new biology. In this dramatic and suspenseful narrative, Jonathan Weiner gives us a remarkable portrait of science and medicine today. We learn about gene therapy, stem cells, brain vaccines, and other novel treatments for such nerve-death diseases as ALS, Alzheimer's, and Parkinson's -- diseases that afflict millions, and touch the lives of many more.It turns out that the author has a personal stake in the story as well. When he met the Heywood brothers, his own mother was dying of a rare nerve-death disease. The Heywoods' gene therapist offered to try to save her, too.\"The Heywoods' story taught me many things about the nature of healing in the new millennium,\" Weiner writes.","primaryTopic":"Medicine, Health & the Body","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Medicine & Public Health","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Medicine & Public Health","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Medicine & Public Health","mappedSub